h Many Factorials"} :step/id #uuid "6eb5e047-89fd-5094-98b2-bfe287784d92" :step/math-academy-id 20564} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180382 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180676 :tutorial/content "Factorials can be applied to variables, too. To manipulate a factorial expression involving a variable, we just need to remember that the variable represents a number, and the previous number can be obtained by subtracting $1$ from the variable.\n\nSo, in the same way that we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5! & =5\\cdot \\overset{4!}{\\overset{⏞}{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe also have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n! & =n\\cdot \\overset{(n-1)!}{\\overset{⏞}{(n-1)\\cdot (n-2)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =n\\cdot (n-1)!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes some positive integer.\n\nLikewise, in the same way that we have\n\n$$\n5! = 5 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 3!\n$$\n\nwe also have\n\n$$\nx! = x \\cdot (x-1) \\cdot (x-2)!\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "d18ec8c1-f094-5d15-ac9e-61e003934f78" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3885 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "455da497-9e49-58fc-a08d-ffe137a6ee4f" :step/math-academy-id 22949 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180478}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180478 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179730 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179592 :question/id #uuid "bcdea8ab-4c41-5d45-b62f-a1f2dc9f83e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9520"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049341}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179997} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179998} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233344} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233345} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233346} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233347}] :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"} :step/id #uuid "c241e16e-442e-51d2-908a-ad376a91f3f9" :step/math-academy-id 35638 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 